{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED on the three scoped repairs at exact clean head 51fb936e23b9e24ab59aee6df11d03a35389ba3e, against request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2f1eeb7bb102d7250cbeb784d58cc28eab7fc672, promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:658c71877a0366d1c1d553526a78450020323ba5, and artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:60df97d546d410358403809f506bd1dbc7a82b34. The deliberately unrepaired descriptive-edge model was not judged as part of this verdict.\n\nTwo repairs close cleanly. Succession now sees every earlier live artifact at the exact path, so retiring the immediate predecessor no longer hides an older live one. UnableToFlare now covers empty bases and all-unresolvable bases while one resolvable basis is a positive control. The fold proves the premise directly: decideSupersede returns ineffective when the target is unknown, while any event present in byID can be an effective target for its author or a ratifier.\n\nOne aggregate case remains wrong. OmittedSupersessions counts every unretired artifact except the last ever seen at a path, even when every later successor is retired. Independent executable probe: A is live, B follows at the same path, then B is superseded/withdrawn. A is the only current artifact and there is no live successor requiring A's retirement, but the projection reports one supersession “still owed.” That is not an actionable repair: following the warning would retire the restored current artifact because of a withdrawn replacement. Count an omission only when a relevant later successor remains live, or rename and render this as historical evidence rather than a current owed act; add the retired-last-successor control. The existing mixed-middle test does not cover this direction.\n\nExact-head package tests and make vet pass. Three build-valid mutations were independently checked: limiting succession to the immediate predecessor fails TestOwedSupersessionsDivergeFromRowCount; reverting dangling-basis detection fails TestArtifactCitingOnlyUnresolvableBasesCannotFlare; substituting path count for owed count fails TestStatusPageCountsSuccessionPathsAsWellAsArtifacts. The new retired-successor probe fails with “owed supersessions = 1, want 0.” No merge performed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:60df97d546d410358403809f506bd1dbc7a82b34","head":"51fb936e23b9e24ab59aee6df11d03a35389ba3e","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2f1eeb7bb102d7250cbeb784d58cc28eab7fc672","scope":"three independent repairs only","verdict":"changes-requested"}}